---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HeroFlow from '../components/HeroFlow.astro';
import IntroVideo from '../components/IntroVideo.astro';
import Offer from '../components/Offer.astro';
import IntentTeaser from '../components/IntentTeaser.astro';
import { APP_STORE_URL } from '../consts';
import BookDemo from '../components/BookDemo.astro';

const title = 'QSortby — Sort smarter. Sell more with AI. | Shopify';
const description =
  'Auto-sort Shopify collections by what sells, then upsell in the cart, popup, checkout and thank-you page with offers learned from what your shoppers view, add and buy, re-ranked by why each shopper came. Every sort and every offer measured in your own dashboard.';
import CardViz from '../components/CardViz.astro';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap herogrid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        {/* The brand tagline, verbatim (consts.TAGLINE): the dot is always
            brand green and the line is never translated. */}
        <h1><span class="h1l">Sort smarter<em style="color:var(--green)">.</em></span> <span class="h1l">Sell more with AI<em style="color:var(--green)">.</em></span></h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Collections rank themselves by what is selling. Then AI suggests the right add-on at the moment a shopper is deciding — learned from what your shoppers view, add and buy, re-ranked by why they came, and measured in your own dashboard.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a href={APP_STORE_URL} class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Install free <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
          <BookDemo class="btn btn-line btn-lg">Book a demo</BookDemo>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-viz"><HeroFlow /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== INTRO VIDEO =====================
       High on the page — right after the trust bar, before the first wall of
       argument — because a visitor who would rather be shown than told should
       not have to hunt for it. The hero keeps its own trust bar directly beneath
       it; the video takes the next slot.

       Renders only when the asset exists (see public/video/README.md), so the
       page is complete with or without it. -->
  <IntroVideo duration="1:58" />

  <!-- ===================== WHAT YOU GET =====================
       The three jobs the app does, each with its own short case and picture —
       merchandising, personalization, upsell. Sits right under the intro
       video: whoever just watched the whole journey lands here to see the
       three buckets it came from. See src/components/Offer.astro. -->
  <Offer />

  <!-- ===================== SHOWS ITS WORK =====================
       Sits immediately after the console because the console raises the exact
       fear this answers: "so it rearranges my storefront on its own?"

       ── This is the differentiating section on the page. ──
       It was framed as "You stay in control" — a reassurance. That framing
       undersold it. Auto-sorting, sold-out demotion and rules on sales/margin/
       stock are the whole category now; a merchant comparing apps in the App
       Store sees the same bullet list on every listing. What none of them offer
       is the ability to CHECK the result — why a product landed where it did,
       what the last run changed, whether it ran at all this morning, and what
       the revenue figure actually means. Those four are the reason to choose
       this app, so they lead here rather than sitting in three separate places.

       Every claim here is a shipped, UNGATED capability, verified in the app
       repo: the per-signal breakdown on the product page (routes/app/products/
       $id.tsx, no plan guard), the before/after preview, manual approval,
       manual membership, sort snapshot + config history, the run/pixel/sync
       state on the app home, and last-touch attribution. Nothing may be added
       here unless a merchant can verify it inside the app on the Free plan. -->
  <section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead ctr shead-lg rv" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
        <h2>If you've said any of these, you're in the right place.</h2>
        <p class="lead-c">Nobody wakes up wanting to re-order a collection. Something looked wrong, and you went looking for a way to stop fixing it by hand.</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="said rv">
        <li>
          <p class="said-q">Sold-out products keep hogging the front row.</p>
          <p class="said-a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7"/></svg><span>Dropped within minutes, and back the moment it's restocked.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="said-q">Our new drops get buried before they have a chance.</p>
          <p class="said-a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7"/></svg><span>How new a product is counts too, so a launch can actually rise.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="said-q">Every visitor sees the exact same order.</p>
          <p class="said-a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7"/></svg><span>A feed built from what this visit is doing. No login needed.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="said-q">I reordered a collection and have no idea if it helped.</p>
          <p class="said-a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7"/></svg><span>The new order runs as an A/B test against the old one.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="said-q">Past a few hundred products, I can't merchandise by hand.</p>
          <p class="said-a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7"/></svg><span>Set the rule once. Every collection, and every new product, follows it.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="said-q">Nobody can tell me why a product ranks where it does.</p>
          <p class="said-a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.2 4.2L19 7"/></svg><span>The rule behind every position, in plain language, yours to change.</span></p>
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== LEARNS FROM YOUR SHOPPERS =====================
       The machine-learning story, told at the level a merchant can verify in
       the app, with its status said out loud. Three cards:
         1. bought-together pairs — the nightly market-basket rebuild from
            customer_order_lines (apps/api services/affinity; a pair counts from
            two orders). The API's isAffinityRanked flag is NOT merchant-visible,
            so the card must not claim the app "says so" when a list is padded.
         2. the live "bought together" goes-with source — switches a partner only
            after a clear margin and a week's dwell; an unsellable partner is
            replaced at once (services/pair-resolution).
         3. the per-intent learned picks — computed nightly, held in TESTING
            until they beat the store's own best sellers on visits they did not
            learn from, three nights running (packages/shared intent-fit), shown
            as "Ready" in the Intent tab and NOT used to rank. Do not move that
            card to "live" until the app serves it by default.
       Status words match /features/intent-ai: Live / Testing. -->
  <section class="sec mintband">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead ctr shead-lg rv" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Learns from your shoppers</span>
        <h2>Upsells that learn from your store — and have to prove it first.</h2>
        <p class="lead-c">No bundle list to maintain. QSortby reads what your shoppers actually view, add and buy together, keeps those offers current as behavior changes, and holds anything it learns in testing until it beats what you already have.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bento rv">
        <div class="b">
          <span class="kicker">Live</span>
          <CardViz kind="pairs" />
          <h3>Bought, added and viewed together</h3>
          <p>Every night QSortby rebuilds which products your customers buy, add and view together from your own orders, cart adds and product views. A bought-together pair has to show up in more than one order to count, so one unusual basket never becomes a recommendation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="b">
          <span class="kicker">Live</span>
          <CardViz kind="goeswith" />
          <h3>Goes-with that keeps up with your orders</h3>
          <p>A goes-with rule can follow your live purchases: a partner is swapped only once a challenger has clearly overtaken it and held that lead for a week, so your product pages are not reshuffled by one busy weekend. A partner that stops being sellable is replaced without waiting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="b">
          <span class="kicker">Testing</span>
          <CardViz kind="proof" />
          <h3>Learning that has to beat your best sellers</h3>
          <p>For each reason a visit comes — a gift, a replacement, a treat — QSortby learns which products those shoppers go on to buy. Those picks stay in testing, measured against your own best sellers on visits they never learned from, and are shown to you in the Intent tab as <b>Ready</b> only once they clearly win, three nights in a row. Nothing learned ranks your storefront without you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="rv" style="margin-top:1.5rem;text-align:center;font-size:var(--fs-caption);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/features/upsell-blocks">How Upsell AI works →</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="/features/intent-ai">How Intent AI learns →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== INTENT AI =====================
       One band, linking to /features/intent-ai. After "in the right place"
       because that section's third card ("Every visitor sees the exact same
       order") is the problem Intent AI answers. Growth-only, and says so —
       see src/components/IntentTeaser.astro. -->
  <IntentTeaser />

  <!-- ===================== FINAL CTA ===================== -->
  <section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta rv">
        <h2>Let your storefront optimize itself — and <em>prove it did.</em></h2>
        <p>Install free, run it on one collection, and read the attributed revenue in your own dashboard.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta" style="justify-content:center">
          <a href={APP_STORE_URL} class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Install free <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
          <BookDemo class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Book a demo</BookDemo>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
